Quoting  Rast  <rast2@hotmail.com>:
>These four possible outcomes are not very different, so let's look at the 
>expected values:
>Wishing for +2: +10.6 AC and MR
>Wishing for +3: +10.8 AC and MR
>So clearly one should go for the slightly higher expected value.

Assuming that the utility of each point of AC is equal. Which it isn't;
once you're past the AC 0 discontinuity, each additional point of AC probably
has lesser utility than the previous one.

[Don't look at the raw numbers on to-hit and damage; ask yourself, what's
the chance I'll die by having AC -10 not AC -11? What about AC -11 vs AC
-12?]

This is much more obvious with wishes for scrolls where the utility of
each additional scroll of charging after the one that recharges the wand
of wishing is going to be less - even if you have a second WoW, your first
round of wishes is much more likely to make the difference between life
and death.
